+++
title: The awkward cases
+++
% // A site made of the inputs that were bugs.
% //
% // §4 called this the most valuable single addition, and the argument is
% // that every unit test here passes against an engine that still builds the
% // wrong SITE: what these files broke was identity, ordering and the walk,
% // which only a whole build shows. Each line below names the finding it is
% // standing on, and check-sites builds the lot both ways and diffs.
%
% // B1: a .yaml whose first line is `---` was read as a document separator and
% // desynchronised every identity after it. B2: an empty .mdy and a
% // whitespace-only one shifted every later document by one. If either is
% // wrong, `city.yaml`'s fields land on some other file's record and this
% // query answers with the wrong one — or with nothing.
% const cities = $.find({ role: "city" })
% $.emit("cities.json", JSON.stringify(cities.map((c) => c.who + "/" + c.era)))
%
% // B8 — a file name carrying a `"` — is NOT here, and deliberately: Windows
% // forbids a quote in a file name, so committing one would break the
% // checkout on a platform this project builds for. It is covered by
% // test/engine.c, which makes the file at run time in a temp directory,
% // which is the only way to test it on a repository that has to clone
% // everywhere.
%
% // The `+++` inside a block scalar is data, not a front-matter marker.
% const notes = $.find({ kind: "note" })
% $.emit("note.json", JSON.stringify(notes.map((n) => n.body)))
%
% // B3: a .md reached through $.render came back an empty or wrong token, and
% // the same document through $.text is the other half of that path.
% $.emit("prose.html", $.render({ path: "pages/prose.md" }))
% $.emit("prose.txt", $.text({ path: "pages/prose.md" }))
%
% // B20: a table of seventy columns, where the buffer held sixty-four.
% $.emit("wide.html", $.render({ path: "pages/wide.md" }))
%
% // B11: a .tif whose header points its IFD past the end of the file. It is a
% // real file and still gets a record; what it must not get is width/height
% // read from off the end of it.
% const img = $.findOne({ ext: ".tif" })
% $.emit("image.json", JSON.stringify({ name: img.name, w: img.width ?? null, h: img.height ?? null }))
%
% // The whole set, in order, which is what B1 and B2 moved.
% $.emit("order.json", JSON.stringify($.find({}).map((d) => d.path)))

= {{ res.data.title }}

{{ cities.length }} city, {{ $.count }} documents.
